  "facts": [
    "Both roots used gpt-6.1-sol high; all three direct helpers used gpt-6.1-sol medium in every observed turn context.",
    "All three root spawns explicitly set fork_turns=none. No helper spawned descendants. Fresh history does not eliminate repeated runtime instructions.",
    "swarm_hotel, swarm_studio and swarm_landscape each owned complete page markup, styles, interaction, two images, manifest and focused checks. Coherent page ownership replaced pilot page-lead plus small nested reservation helper.",
    "swarm_primary implemented the root portfolio, strengthened structural/resource integration checks and configured verification profiles, reviewed source and images, and requested whitespace-name and long-input fixes. This was useful integration work as well as coordination.",
    "swarm_primary has six send_message calls, three followup_task calls and one list_agents call. Hotel has two task starts; landscape has three, including focused follow-up fixes.",
    "Helpers read BRIEF and imagegen skill; hotel and studio also read project contracts in broad first retrievals. Initial AGENTS/runtime instructions are repeated across fresh sessions; character measurements are not tokenizer-equivalent.",
    "Rendered browser inspection was blocked in both modes by browser launch restrictions. Native image inspection and source/interaction checks cannot establish rendered visual quality.",
    "No retained tool text contains base64 image data markers. Image results were stored and metadata/files handled without the pilot full-result text print pattern. This does not by itself measure all serialization costs.",
    "Retained textual tool outputs total 200,065 characters across the swarm versus 57,552 for single. Large outputs include a roughly 40k-character root client-source read; broad BRIEF/skill retrievals contribute roughly 25k per helper. These are retained text characters, not billed token counts."
  ],
  "inferences": [
    "Swarm coding proxy is higher primarily because three additional sessions process their own repeatedly cached contexts; unlike pilot, even primary input grows. Arithmetic isolates contributions but does not causally identify why each request was needed.",
    "Direct complete-page ownership and medium helper effort plausibly reduce coordination/capability overhead relative to pilot, but changed brief, artifacts, run conditions and stochastic behavior prevent a causal policy-gain claim.",
    "Full-page helper ownership is substantial independent work; integration and follow-up checks have legitimate purpose. Their net value requires quality and time evidence, not token totals alone."
  ],
